@startuml sequence-diagram-02
title Sequence diagram 02
hide footbox

skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #005b72
    ParticipantFontColor #ffffff
    ArrowColor #235872
    LifeLineBorderColor #005b72
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #005b72
}


participant "Customer" as Customer
participant "Frontend" as Frontend
participant "B F F" as BFF
participant "Ecommerce" as Ecommerce
participant "Mock Payment Gateway" as MockGateway
participant "Mock Payment Service" as MockPayment
participant "Postgre" as Postgre

== Pago ==

note over BFF,Ecommerce
El frontend inicia el proceso de pago enviando un payment-attempt al BFF que realiza la llamada a ecommerce.
Este registra el intento de pago en su base de datos y hace una llamada REST al servicio de pago mockeado
para registrar el intento de pago en la pasarela mockeada.
El servicio de pago mockeado devuelve una URL de redirección a la pasarela mockeada.

El navegador del cliente es redirigido a la pasarela mockeada que llama a la API del servicio de pago
mockeado. Este notifica a ecommerce mediante el callback, que actualiza el estado de la Order a pagado.
end note


Customer -> Frontend : Seleccionar método de pago
activate Customer
activate Frontend
Frontend -> BFF : POST /checkout/{id}/payment-attempts
activate BFF
BFF -> Ecommerce : POST /api/v1/orders/{id}/payment-attempts
activate Ecommerce
Ecommerce --> Postgre : Registrar intento de pago (PENDING)
activate Postgre
Postgre --> Ecommerce : OK
deactivate Postgre
Ecommerce -> MockPayment : Registrar intento en pasarela mock (REST)
activate MockPayment
MockPayment --> Postgre : Guardar intento de pago
activate Postgre
Postgre --> MockPayment : OK
deactivate Postgre
MockPayment --> Ecommerce : redirectUrl
deactivate MockPayment
Ecommerce --> BFF : redirectUrl + attemptId
deactivate Ecommerce
BFF --> Frontend : redirectUrl + attemptId
deactivate BFF
Frontend --> Customer : Redirigir a pasarela de pago
deactivate Frontend
deactivate Customer

Customer -> MockGateway : Accede a la pasarela de pago (browser redirect)
activate Customer
activate MockGateway
MockGateway -> MockPayment : POST /api/v1/payment-attempts/{attemptId}/pay
activate MockPayment
MockPayment --> Postgre : Actualizar intento → SUCCESS
activate Postgre
Postgre --> MockPayment : OK
deactivate Postgre
MockPayment -> Ecommerce : POST /api/v1/payment-callbacks/mock
activate Ecommerce
Ecommerce -> Ecommerce : Verificar pago y activar saga
Ecommerce --> Postgre : Actualizar Order → PAID
activate Postgre
Postgre --> Ecommerce : OK
deactivate Postgre
Ecommerce --> MockPayment : 202 Accepted
deactivate Ecommerce
MockPayment --> MockGateway : redirectUrl con status=SUCCESS
deactivate MockPayment
MockGateway --> Customer : Redirigir a página de resultado
deactivate MockGateway
deactivate Customer

@enduml